IV. RIGHT-INVARIANT EKF FOR DOUBLE LOWER KINEMATICS-BASED KALMAN MODEL
In practical realization, the measurements from IMU sensors
always contains the gyroscope and accelerometer biases,
desiring additional modeling. There are two approaches to
handle these appended states. The one is to set the biases as
constant parameters. Assume that they usually change over a
longer period of time than the experiment[20]. Then we can
calibrate these biases in a separate experiment. Another one
method regards the biases as a part of the estimated states. Then
the deviation can be estimated simultaneously while estimating
the attitude. The latter scheme is adopted in this paper, because
the on-line real-time compensation of the influence of deviation
can improve the accuracy of attitude estimation. Once the
deviation is taken into account, no Lie group can satisfy the
group affine properties of the dynamic equation[21]. Even
though several theoretical characters are no longer valid, it is
still possible to design an “augmented InEKF” that still
outperforms the “standard EKF”[22]. Due to that the two
fashions of processing deviation are similar, we only discuss
gyroscope bias in this section for the purpose of saving text space.
