VI. SIMULATION
The IMU utilized to measure the 10 freedoms of lower joints,
is equipped on thighs, calves, and feet of double lower limbs.
Combining the IMU fixed on waist to provide angular velocity
and linear acceleration measurements, the kinematics of
pedestrian locomotion is computed.
The EKF trial proceeded the same specification with InEKF
run. The proposed algorithm and EKF flow were operated in
MATLAB. The computation time of single filter loop for both
algorithms was approximately 1ms, possessing low calculation
consumption. The associated parameter initialization and
specification are listed in Table I.
