VII. CONCLUSIONS
Exercising simulation results on a right-invariant form of
the extended Kalman filter, this article derived an motion state
observer for double lower-limbs kinematics of pedestrian. With
available IMU sensors on pedestrian’s waist and lower limbs,
the developed scheme has the capability to improve the
accuracy and reliability of state estimation of pedestrian. We
also included IMU biases in the state estimator and showed that,
the proposed system has better performance than that of a
commonly used EKF. Future work includes integration of the
state estimation developed in this work to operate and even
more complicated action in experiment, constructing a outdoor
system.
